# Problems to practice

## Where lower/upper_bound is the central technique
- Binary Search (704) warmup, can be done with lower_bound
- Search Insert Position (35) literally lower_bound
- Find First and Last Position of Element in Sorted Array (34) lower_bound + upper_bound
- Count of Smaller Numbers After Self (315) counting with bounds after sorting
- Kth Missing Positive Number (1539)
- Time Based Key-Value Store (981) upper_bound over timestamps (Two Sigma style)
- Find Smallest Letter Greater Than Target (744) upper_bound directly
- Search a 2D Matrix (74) treat as sorted, binary search
- H-Index II (275)

## Where it is an auxiliary step inside a bigger algorithm
- Longest Increasing Subsequence (300) lower_bound to place each number, O(n log n)
- Russian Doll Envelopes (354) sort, then LIS with lower_bound
- Maximum Length of Pair Chain (646)
- Non-overlapping Intervals (435) sort, then greedy with search
- Longest Increasing Subsequence variants and patience-sorting problems
- Aggressive Cows / capacity-style "binary search on the answer" problems
- Split Array Largest Sum (410) binary search on the answer range
- Koko Eating Bananas (875) binary search on the answer

Note: the "binary search on the answer" problems (410, 875, aggressive cows)
usually need a hand-written binary search because the check is a custom predicate,
not a >= lookup. Good to know they are the same family even when the library
version does not fit.
